<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luoyang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luoyang is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> valley of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and one of China's ancient capitals. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> it served as the eastern capital alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>. Both cities were sacked during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huang-chao-rebellion">Huang Chao Rebellion</a> of 874 to 884, a blow from which Tang central government never recovered.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luoyang.jpg" alt="Luoyang" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rialfver Original uploader was Rialfver at nl.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Longmen_Grottoes_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
